# web-audio-separation

Music source separation (vocal removal / demixing) that runs entirely in the browser, powered by ONNX Runtime Web.

This is a TypeScript port of python-audio-separator, reimplemented so separation models can run client-side with no server or Python required.

...

## Usage

```typescript
import { createSeparator } from 'web-audio-separation';

// Pick a registered model (see below for available models).
const separator = createSeparator('UVR_MDXNET_KARA_2');

// Downloads the ONNX model from Hugging Face (cached in CacheStorage after
// the first run) and loads it into an ONNX Runtime session.
await separator.loadModel();

// Accepts a URL (including an object URL from a <input type="file">) and
// returns object URLs for the separated stems, ready to use in an <audio>
// element or download link.
const fileInput = document.querySelector('input[type="file"]') as HTMLInputElement;
const objectUrl = URL.createObjectURL(fileInput.files![0]);
const stemUrls = await separator.separate(objectUrl);

console.log(stemUrls); // e.g. ["blob:http://.../abc", "blob:http://.../def"]
```

### Available models

Currently only models built on the MDX architecture are supported.

| Name | Task | Size | Primary stem |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `UVR_MDXNET_KARA_2` | Karaoke: keeps backing vocals in the instrumental | ~30MB | Instrumental |
| `UVR-MDX-NET-Voc_FT` | Removes all vocals (lead + backing) | ~67MB | Vocals |
| `Kim_Vocal_2` | Removes all vocals (lead + backing) | ~67MB | Vocals |
| `UVR_MDXNET_Main` | Removes all vocals (lead + backing) | ~67MB | Vocals |

`createSeparator` looks up the model in `MODEL_REGISTRY`, wires up its download URL and stem names, and returns an `MDXSeparator`. It accepts optional config for both the common separator behavior and MDX-specific architecture parameters.

