content.text:
Fixed and the dev server is back up at **http://127.0.0.1:5173** — reload the app and your playlists should appear.

**What was wrong:** `getPlaylists()` was written as if `/me/playlists` returned each playlist wrapped in a `{ track: … }` object — that shape actually belongs to the *tracks inside a playlist* endpoint. Spotify's `/me/playlists` returns Playlist objects directly in `items`, so the line `if (item.track) out.push(item.track)` matched nothing and silently produced an empty list. The request itself succeeded (that's why you saw no error toast), it just threw away the results.

**The fix** in `src/lib/api.ts`:

```ts
const res = await request<Paged<Playlist | null>>(path);
for (const item of res.items) {
  if (item?.id) out.push(item);
}
```

This covers both your created and followed playlists (all pages up to 1,000), skips any null entries, and keeps pagination intact.

Build is clean. Since the old server had been cancelled by the app restart, I started a fresh one — same URL, `http://127.0.0.1:5173`. If your playlists still don't show after a reload, tell me and I'll trace the actual `/me/playlists` response next.
